      "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7802122/",
      "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fe8b10a06af3edef\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe low frequency of hypokalemia in this group of eating disordered outpatients suggests that routine electrolyte determination is a poor screening tool for occult or denied bulimia. Hypokalemia occurred almost invariably in lower-weight bulimic (or anorectic/bulimic) patients who were vomiting and/ …\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fe8b10a06af3edef\">>>",
