    {
      "title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"86d732681cdb10e3\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nManaging Low Potassium (Hypokalemia) | Eating Disorder Refeeding\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"86d732681cdb10e3\">>>",
      "url": "https://www.acute.org/resource/managing-potassium-eating-disorder-refeeding",
      "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"617bb777be77e3e5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThere, experts across several disciplines carefully initiate nutritional replenishment tailored to each patient’s unique needs and risk factors, frequently monitoring blood chemistry and vitals, addressing complications immediately and aggressively replenishing these electrolytes orally or intravenously as the clinical situation dictates. For more information on managing potassium during eating disorder refeeding, contact us.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"617bb777be77e3e5\">>>",
      "published": "February 26, 2021",
      "siteName": "www.acute.org"
    },
    {
      "title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5e083137631dbb54\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nHypokalemia in patients with anorexia nervosa during refeeding is associated with binge–purge behavior, lower body mass index, and hypoalbuminemia | Journal of Eating Disorders | Full Text\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5e083137631dbb54\">>>",
